1
00:00:00,050 --> 00:00:06,043
Before DRIP, though, came the summer single that taught the fanbase how to miss a song on purpose.

2
00:00:06,043 --> 00:00:13,273
Forever was built light — retro synth, open vowels, a chorus that asked to be sung in a stadium parking lot.

3
00:00:13,273 --> 00:00:24,690
It was also, quietly, a demo of the group's post-hiatus chemistry: parts arranged to interlock seven ways, with the seventh voice threaded through harmonies instead of stacked above them.

4
00:00:24,690 --> 00:00:28,969
Arrangers write differently when the full instrument finally exists.

